WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.325
Lesson 0.8.

00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:05.550
Your security baseline, and the language of DeFi.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.519
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:09.647
able to lock in the habits that prevent

00:00:09.647 --> 00:00:11.828
most losses, and learn the words used in

00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:13.105
the rest of the program.

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:15.695
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.695 --> 00:00:17.380
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.905
Then, your checklist.

00:00:18.905 --> 00:00:21.067
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.652
First, never share your seed phrase.

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:26.292
No real person or company

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.917
will ever ask for it.

00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:30.634
Next, Bookmark the sites you use; never

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:33.311
reach them from ads, DMs or emails.

00:00:33.311 --> 00:00:35.858
Then, Nobody legitimate DMs you first

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:38.906
offering help, investments or "recovery".

00:00:38.906 --> 00:00:41.511
Also, Guaranteed returns are a scam.

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:42.536
Always.

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:44.994
On top of that, Read every wallet prompt

00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:47.511
before approving: what, how much, to whom.

00:00:48.811 --> 00:00:49.965
And Test first with a

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:51.786
small amount on anything new.

00:00:51.786 --> 00:00:53.609
Plus, use a hardware wallet once

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:55.346
the amount matters to you.

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:57.979
One more: keep devices updated, and use

00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:00.781
a separate browser profile for crypto.

00:01:00.781 --> 00:01:02.794
One more: keep records of every

00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:04.856
buy, sell, transfer and fee.

00:01:04.856 --> 00:01:07.871
And finally, if something feels urgent, stop.

00:01:07.871 --> 00:01:11.061
Scammers create urgency; real opportunities wait.

00:01:12.361 --> 00:01:15.571
Address: your public "account number" on a blockchain.

00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:17.877
Seed phrase: 12–24 words that recreate

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.069
your wallet's keys. Never share.

00:01:20.069 --> 00:01:20.410
Private key: the secret that signs

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.149
transactions (your seed phrase generates it).

00:01:21.149 --> 00:01:23.302
Custody: who holds the keys: an

00:01:23.302 --> 00:01:26.494
exchange (custodial) or you (self-custody).

00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:28.463
Gas: the network fee for a

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.754
transaction, paid in the network's token.

00:01:31.754 --> 00:01:36.089
Network / chain: A blockchain, e.g.

00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:41.023
Ethereum, Arbitrum, Base.

00:01:42.323 --> 00:01:44.615
Layer 2 (L2): A cheaper, faster

00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:47.278
network built on top of Ethereum.

00:01:47.278 --> 00:01:49.696
Token: A unit of value on a

00:01:49.696 --> 00:01:54.186
blockchain, e.g. USDC. Stablecoin: A token designed

00:01:54.186 --> 00:01:57.508
to hold a steady value, usually $1.

00:01:57.508 --> 00:01:59.472
Smart contract: A program on a

00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:02.053
blockchain that follows fixed rules.

00:02:02.053 --> 00:02:06.298
DEX: Decentralised exchange: swap tokens from your wallet.

00:02:06.298 --> 00:02:08.156
Approval: Permission for an app

00:02:08.156 --> 00:02:09.608
to move a specific token.

00:02:10.908 --> 00:02:13.108
Block explorer: A website that

00:02:13.108 --> 00:02:16.318
shows every transaction (e.g. Etherscan).

00:02:16.318 --> 00:02:19.176
Testnet / faucet: A practice blockchain /

00:02:19.176 --> 00:02:21.518
a site giving free test coins.

00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:26.878
APY: Annual percentage yield: yearly return including compounding.

00:02:26.878 --> 00:02:29.490
Liquidity: how easily something can be bought

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.663
or sold without moving the price.

00:02:31.663 --> 00:02:36.073
KYC: ID checks required by regulated exchanges.

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:39.166
2FA: Two-factor authentication: a second

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:41.203
proof of identity at login.

00:02:42.503 --> 00:02:43.963
Here's your checklist.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.498
Do it now, for real.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.878
First, I've read the 10

00:02:46.878 --> 00:02:48.673
rules and can repeat them.

00:02:48.673 --> 00:02:52.058
Next, Separate browser profile set up for crypto.

00:02:52.058 --> 00:02:54.753
And finally, I know every word in the glossary.

00:02:56.053 --> 00:02:57.263
Question 1.

00:02:57.263 --> 00:03:00.438
Someone offers a "guaranteed 2% a day".

00:03:00.438 --> 00:03:01.163
What is it?

00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:07.298
The answer: A scam.

00:03:07.298 --> 00:03:09.323
Guaranteed returns don't exist.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.868
Question 2.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:12.743
What's gas?

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.162
The answer: The network fee for a

00:03:19.162 --> 00:03:21.573
transaction, paid in the network's token.

00:03:22.873 --> 00:03:24.143
Question 3.

00:03:24.143 --> 00:03:26.214
A message says your wallet will be

00:03:26.214 --> 00:03:28.703
"suspended" unless you act in 1 hour.

00:03:28.703 --> 00:03:29.553
What do you do?

00:03:33.973 --> 00:03:35.568
The answer: Stop.

00:03:35.568 --> 00:03:37.598
Urgency is a scam tactic.

00:03:37.598 --> 00:03:39.573
Wallets can't be suspended; check

00:03:39.573 --> 00:03:41.838
only through bookmarked official sites.

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:46.358
First, Password manager installed; master password

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.614
written down and stored safely.

00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:53.739
Next, Email secured: unique password + authenticator-app 2FA.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:56.774
Then, Authenticator app installed on your phone.

00:03:56.774 --> 00:04:01.104
Also, Exchange chosen (legally available to you, reputable).

00:04:01.104 --> 00:04:03.085
On top of that, Exchange

00:04:03.085 --> 00:04:05.699
account opened and KYC completed.

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:10.532
And Exchange 2FA on (authenticator or security

00:04:10.532 --> 00:04:14.064
key, not SMS); backup codes stored offline.

00:04:14.064 --> 00:04:17.969
And finally, Anti-phishing code and withdrawal allowlist switched on.

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:21.131
First, Deposited a small learning

00:04:21.131 --> 00:04:23.074
amount by the cheapest method.

00:04:23.074 --> 00:04:25.211
Next, Bought a little ETH

00:04:25.211 --> 00:04:28.059
(gas) and some USDC (practice).

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:29.934
Then, Tried a limit order.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:32.277
And finally, Started a simple records

00:04:32.277 --> 00:04:34.806
sheet: date, action, amount, price, fees.

00:04:36.105 --> 00:04:38.044
First, Wallet installed from the

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.930
official website (separate browser profile).

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.169
Next, New seed phrase written on

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:45.980
paper/metal, in order; never digital.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.340
Then, Restore test passed: same address appears.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.489
And finally, Wallet address saved in the password

00:04:52.489 --> 00:04:55.450
manager's notes (address only, never the seed).

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.055
First, Network chosen (low-fee L2 supported by your wallet).

00:05:01.055 --> 00:05:03.894
Next, Test withdrawal (e.g. $10

00:05:03.894 --> 00:05:06.500
of ETH) sent and received.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.630
Then, Remaining learning funds sent;

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.715
address added to the allowlist.

00:05:10.715 --> 00:05:13.645
And finally, Transfer found on a block explorer.

00:05:14.945 --> 00:05:17.869
First, Sepolia test network added; free

00:05:17.869 --> 00:05:19.850
test ETH from a faucet.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.865
Next, one practice transaction on the testnet.

00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:24.837
Then, one tiny real swap on

00:05:24.837 --> 00:05:27.250
an L2 with a limited approval.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.830
And finally, Approval revoked afterwards.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.335
All ticked?

00:05:32.335 --> 00:05:35.790
You're ready for Module 1 — Foundations & Safety.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.475
First, the 10 rules read and understood.

00:05:38.475 --> 00:05:42.190
Next, Sites bookmarked; no links from ads or DMs.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.179
Then, Hardware wallet ordered from the

00:05:44.179 --> 00:05:46.315
maker (when the amount will matter).

00:05:46.315 --> 00:05:48.570
And finally, Records sheet up to date.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.385
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:55.570
Next up, Lesson 1.0: Mastery Starter.
